{"page_id": "olmo_table_tests-6767787c7d1b64b777ddab83e3e88569ae24_pg1-p1", "markdown": "# Program Planner\n\n2019-2020\n\nBUSINESS TRANSFER PATHWAY\n\nItasca Community College\n\nDegree:\n\nLength:\n\nAssociate of Science\n\n60 semester credits\n\nThe Associate of Science Degree in Business Transfer Pathway is designed to provide a strong foundation of knowledge and skills for students interested in transferring on to earn a four-year degree in business, for those planning on entering the workforce, or for those starting their own business.\n\ncourse credits that directly transfer to designated business bachelor's degree programs at Minnesota State universities. The\n\nMinnesota State universities enter the university with junior-year status.\n\na related field. Universities within the Minnesota State system include Bemidji State University; Metropolitan State University;\n\nMinnesota State University, Mankato; Minnesota State University Moorhead; Southwest Minnesota State University; St. Cloud State University, and Winona State University.\n\nThe following minimum requirements must be completed:\n\nSpecific program requirements\n\nAn Associate of Science degree requires a minimum of 30 credits selected from at least six of the ten goal areas of the Minnesota Transfer Curriculum (MnTC)\n\nA minimum of 20 credits must be completed at Itasca Community College\n\nStudents are recommended to take a course in MnTC Goal Area 3 and a course in MnTC Goal Area 6.\n\nBus\n\nEcon Engl Goal Goal\n\n1201\n\n2101\n\n1101\n\n1-10\n\n1-10\n\nFall Semester\n\nIntro to Business Macroeconomics\n\nComposition I\n\nGeneral Education\n\nGeneral Education\n\n3\n\nBus\n\nEcon\n\nEngi CSci\n\nSpch\n\n2102\n\n2102\n\n1113\n\n1140\n\n1101\n\nSpring Semester\n\nPrinciples of Mgmt Microeconomics or 1105\n\nBusiness Computers or 1105 or 1111\n\n15-16\n\nAcct Bus\n\nMath\n\nPhil Goal\n\n2015\n\n2108\n\n1111\n\n1111\n\n1-10\n\nFall Semester\n\nFinancial Accounting\n\nPrinciples of Marketing\n\nCollege Algebra\n\nEthics\n\nGeneral Education\n\n43333\n\nAcct Bus\n\nMath Goal\n\n2020\n\n1215\n\n1105\n\n1-10\n\nSpring Semester\n\nManagerial Accounting\n\nBusiness Law\n\nElementary Statistics\n\nGeneral Education\n\n16\n\n33333\n\n15\n\n4343\n\n14\n\nconditions of employment, personnel practices, or access to and participation in, procrams, services, and activtles with repard to race, sex color, creed, relelon, ape, nationa origin, disability, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or membership or activity in a local commission as defined by aw, This intormation is ava able in alterative tormat upon advance request by contactine Ann Vidovic, 14 Backes Student Center, annvidoviceitascaccedu, 218 322-2433 or 1-800-996-6422 ext. 2433. This docurent is available in alternative formats to individuals with disabilities. Consumers with hearing or speech disabilities may contact us via their preferred Telecommunications Relay Service. 02/2016", "width": 1700, "height": 2200, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "Program Planner", "bbox": {"x": 1283.0188676775188, "y": 114.58333329752601, "width": 325.33692722371967, "height": 45.833333333333414}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2019-2020", "bbox": {"x": 1420.3943851837655, "y": 164.5404147642929, "width": 183.46998929334777, "height": 37.58583704630516}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "BUSINESS TRANSFER PATHWAY", "bbox": {"x": 274.9326143261455, "y": 247.49999998702827, "width": 728.5714285714287, "height": 41.2500000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Itasca Community College", "bbox": {"x": 270.35040412356136, "y": 320.8333332969576, "width": 485.71428571428567, "height": 45.833333333333414}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Degree:", "bbox": {"x": 100.80862509827043, "y": 403.33333327604157, "width": 114.55525606469004, "height": 27.500000000000146}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Length:", "bbox": {"x": 100.80862510781672, "y": 444.5833332760417, "width": 109.9